---
title: Noise
---
Smooth random values from −1 to 1 at every point, most often read as altitude to make an overworld [[t:149-151 t:162]].

## The rule
```text
for every tile: n = fractal noise at the tile's position, from -1 to 1
height:    brightness = (n + 1) / 2
overworld: water if n < 0, grass if n < 0.5, otherwise mountain
zoom:      sample positions are multiplied by a scale that shrinks
double:    a second, finer noise is mixed in as the scale shrinks
```

The demos use fractal simplex noise, the first one too, though it is named for Perlin [[c10:14-15]]. The talk gives the green band as altitudes from 0 to 0.75 [[t:164-165]]. Its code draws mountain from 0.5, and 0.75 is there only in the water’s color [[c11:31-44]].

